ed_at":"2026-04-30T16:01:54Z","closed_at":"2026-04-30T16:00:55Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in: \n  - v4.7.beta1.official [1c8cc9e7e]\n  - v4.6.2.stable.official [71f334935]\n  - v4.4.1.stable.official [49a5bc7b6]\n\n(other versions not tested, but the problem exists probably since 4.0, maybe even earlier)\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.4.1.stable - Windows 11 (build 26200) - Multi-window, 2 monitors - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated AMD Radeon RX 5600 XT (Advanced Micro Devices, Inc.; 32.0.21043.5001) - AMD Ryzen 7 3800X 8-Core Processor (16 threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen importing an asset (GLTF) that contains two (or more) meshes and generating the collision shapes (physics), the displayed collision shapes are offset if the two meshes don't share the same origin.\n\nI noticed this when importing an asset with a wall (mesh 1, pivot in the middle of the bottom face) and a door in the wall (mesh 2, pivot at the hinges).\n\nI expected the preview of the collision shapes to align with the meshes.\n\n<img width=\"1023\" height=\"627\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d322714b-5c94-4971-ab54-70dd3a9d0b8a\" />\n\nNote that the effectively generated collision shapes align with the meshes - this seems to be a visual issue with the importer.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- Open the import settings for an asset that matches the preconditions\n- activate generate physics for both meshes\n- reimport the asset\n- open the import settings again\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nFor the test project I already changed the import setting for the asset (wall.glb). If you open the wall.glb scene you will directly see the misaligned collision mesh for the wall (and it seems that the collision mesh for the door is not shown)\n\n[bug-report.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/27100231/bug-report.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118967/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118967/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null}